From 46a1cdd099e4d7a00299b474e6d79495c8d0fcd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Axel Huebl <axel.huebl@plasma.ninja>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 21:50:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Tests: SP Tolerances for Strang Split & MAD-X Solenoid

`test_strang_split.py` and `test_madx_min_model.py` were added with
double-precision-only bounds and no precision guard, so both fail in
every single precision job that runs tests.

`test_solenoid_promotion_preserves_the_reference_map` compares the
`Sol` and the promoted `ChrAcc` transfer map at `atol=1.0e-14,
rtol=0`. The map entries are of order one, so in float32 that is two
orders of magnitude below one ulp. Measured over `ks = -2.3 ... 3.0`,
the two maps differ by 3e-8 ... 6e-8, i.e. one to two ulp: they agree
to the last representable bit. Relax to 1.0e-6 (a few ulp) in single
precision, keep 1.0e-14 for double.

`test_split_is_time_symmetric` asserts that tracking through the
reversed chain returns the beam to `1.0e-10`. The forward and the
reversed pass deposit the same particles in a different order, so
their charge densities differ in the last bits and that difference is
carried through the Poisson solve and the gather. In single precision
the floor is set by the summation order of the threaded deposition,
not by the solver tolerance - tightening `mlmg_relative_tolerance`
from 1e-4 to 1e-6 moves the residual by 2%, while the thread count
moves it by two orders:

  OMP threads   1       2       3       4       6       8
  residual      1.6e-7  1.0e-5  3.3e-6  7.1e-7  2.3e-6  7.3e-6

Serial sits at the float32 floor; results are bit-reproducible at a
fixed thread count, so this is a floor and not flakiness. Observed
across platforms: 2.6e-7 ... 1.8e-6 on the conda-forge linux, macOS
and Windows SP jobs, up to 1.0e-5 locally. Relax to 3.0e-5 in single
precision (~3x margin on the widest residual seen), keep 1.0e-10 for
double.

The test stays discriminating: its companion
`test_first_order_composition_is_not_time_symmetric` requires a
residual above 1.0e-4, and the first-order composition misses time
symmetry by 2.7e-2 here - three orders above the relaxed bound.

This follows the existing pattern in e.g. `test_dipedge_ref.py` and
`test_chracc_Ez0.py`.

Found via the conda-forge 26.09 build, where the linux, macOS and
Windows SP jobs all fail these same four cases. Verified on a local
26.09 SINGLE build: 4 failed before, 439 passed / 1 skipped /
3 deselected for the full SP suite with the CI filter after.

